          "turn_index": 2,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What should I use instead for the knees?",
          "answer": "I can give general information, but I need to know what you use now and why you want to change it. Are you using ibuprofen, another medicine, a brace, exercise, or something else? Is the reason side effects, cost, or that it isn't working?\n\nThe osteoarthritis guidance in my reference material describes exercise as the foundation of knee management. It combines strengthening the muscles around the knee, keeping the joint moving, and aerobic activity. Support from a physiotherapist at the start is described as helpful (*lifestyle-osteoarthritis-activity*, *guideline-osteoarthritis-management*). Other non-drug measures listed include:\n\n- **Heat or cold** for symptom relief (*condition-osteoarthritis*)\n- **Braces or orthoses**, described for selected patterns (*guideline-osteoarthritis-management*)\n- **Appropriate footwear** and **walking aids** where they improve function (*condition-osteoarthritis*)\n- **Weight management**, where body weight is above the healthy range. A 5 to 10 percent reduction is described as clinically meaningful (*guideline-osteoarthritis-management*)\n\nThe same guidance describes medicines as add-ons to exercise, not replacements for it. It says topical (applied to the skin) treatments are preferred where the joint is accessible. My search did not return the full section on specific medicines, so I can't name over-the-counter options from my sources. Please ask a pharmacist or doctor which option suits you, and don't stop or change ibuprofen on your own.\n\n**Seek prompt care** if a knee is hot, swollen and very painful, especially with fever. That pattern can suggest infection or crystal arthritis rather than osteoarthritis. Also get assessment if your knee locks or gives way suddenly.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
